// Write elision may not sink a write past a fork.
//
// RC11 forbids r1 = 0: the creation of a thread happens-before everything it
// does, so x := 5 happens-before r1 := x, and x := 0 is coherence-before
// x := 5. Reading x := 0 would put r1 := x fr-before x := 5: an hb;eco cycle.
// Without the first thread's x := 1, MoRDor forbids it too.
//
// sMRD keeps elided writes out of coherence. Eliding x := 5 into the first
// thread's x := 1 moved it past the fork, as a store would move past a
// release: the second thread then no longer happened after it, x := 0 was the
// only write it could read before, and sMRD allowed r1 = 0. A write is now
// elided only into a write on its own thread or after the join.
x := 0;
x := 5;
{
  x := 1;
} ||| {
  r1 := x;
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 0) [sMRD]
